Parse the escaped DQUOTEs Apple writes into property parameter values, e.g. the X-ADDRESS of ``X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;X-ADDRESS=Ayacucho 983\\nPlata Baja \"A\"\\n...`` and the pseudo-quoted ``X-APPLE-ABUID=\"ab://Home\"``. Previously the whole content line failed with ``ValueError`` because the quote tracking was not escape-aware outside quoted values. ``\"`` in an unquoted value now resolves to a literal quote and a ``\"``...``\"``-wrapped value is treated as quoted; a raw, unescaped DQUOTE still raises. I used AI to assist me with this change. @Pushpak731
